    "question": "Consider an arithmetic sequence where \\(u_8=S_8=8\\).\n\nFind the value of the first term, \\(u_1\\), and the value of the common difference, \\(d\\). [5]",
    "hint": "Use the arithmetic-series formula with \\(S_8=8\\), then combine it with the eighth-term condition \\(u_8=8\\).",
    "answer": "**Step 1: Determine the first term**\n\nUsing \\(S_8=8\\) and \\(u_8=8\\),\n\\[\n4(u_1+8)=8. \\qquad \\text{(A1)}\n\\]\nHence\n\\[\nu_1=-6. \\qquad \\text{A1}\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Determine the common difference**\n\nThe eighth-term relation is\n\\[\nu_1+7d=8,\n\\]\nor equivalently \\(4(2u_1+7d)=8\\). (A1)\n\nSubstitute \\(u_1=-6\\): (M1)\n\\[\n-6+7d=8,\n\\]\nso\n\\[\n\\boxed{d=2}. \\qquad \\text{A1}\n\\]\nTherefore, \\(\\boxed{u_1=-6}\\) and \\(\\boxed{d=2}\\).\n\n[5 marks]",
    "whereToLearn": "Mathematics: Analysis and Approaches Standard Level Course Companion · First edition, 2019\n\nWhole question §1.2 Arithmetic and geometric sequences · p. 13\nWhole question §1.3 Arithmetic and geometric series · p. 22",
