    "question": "Consider the function\n\\[\nf(x)=x^2+x+\\frac{50}{x},\\qquad x\\ne0.\n\\]\n\n(a) Find \\(f(1)\\). [2]\n\n(b) Solve \\(f(x)=0\\). [2]\n\nThe graph of \\(f\\) has a local minimum at point \\(A\\).\n\n(c) Find the coordinates of \\(A\\). [2]",
    "hint": "What does direct substitution give first? Which calculator tools can then locate the zero and the turning point?",
    "answer": "(a) Substitute \\(x=1\\): (M1)\n\\[\nf(1)=1^2+1+\\frac{50}{1}.\n\\]\nTherefore,\n\\[\n\\boxed{f(1)=52}. \\qquad \\text{A1 N2}\n\\]\n\n[2 marks]\n\n(b) Using a graphical or numerical solver,\n\\[\nx=-4.04932\\ldots\n\\]\nso\n\\[\n\\boxed{x=-4.05}. \\qquad \\text{A2 N2}\n\\]\n\n[2 marks]\n\n(c) Using a minimum tool on the graph of \\(f\\),\n\\[\nA=(2.76649\\ldots,28.4934\\ldots).\n\\]\nHence,\n\\[\n\\boxed{A=(2.77,28.5)}. \\qquad \\text{A1A1 N2}\n\\]\n\n[2 marks]\n\n> **Note:** This question is from an exam for a previous syllabus and may contain minor differences in marking or structure.",
    "whereToLearn": "Mathematics: Analysis and Approaches Standard Level Course Companion · First edition, 2019\n\n(a) §2.2 Functional notation · p. 69\n(b) §2.3 Drawing graphs of functions · p. 75\n(c) §5.4 Graphical interpretation of first and second derivatives · p. 240",
