    "question": "The functions \\(f\\) and \\(g\\) are defined such that \\(f(x)=\\frac{x+3}{4}\\) and \\(g(x)=8x+5\\).\n\n(a) Show that \\((g\\circ f)(x)=2x+11\\). [2]\n\n(b) Given that \\({(g\\circ f)}^{-1}(a)=4\\), find the value of \\(a\\). [3]",
    "hint": "Which features or conditions of the function can be translated into equations? How do they determine the requested graph or function property?",
    "answer": "(a) attempt to form composition M1\n\ncorrect substitution \\(g(\\frac{x+3}{4})=8(\\frac{x+3}{4})+5\\) A1\n\n\\((g\\circ f)(x)=2x+11\\) AG\n\n[2 marks]\n\nTherefore, the required result is established.\n\n(b) attempt to substitute 4 (seen anywhere) (M1)\n\ncorrect equation \\(a=2\\times 4+11\\) (A1)\n\n\\(a\\) = 19 A1\n\n[3 marks]",
    "whereToLearn": "Mathematics: Analysis and Approaches Standard Level Course Companion · First edition, 2019\n\nWhole question §2.2 Functional notation · p. 69",
    "teacherNote": ""
