    "question": "A data set consisting of \\(16\\) test scores has mean \\(14.5\\) . One test score of \\(9\\) requires a second marking and is removed from the data set.\n\nFind the mean of the remaining \\(15\\) test scores. [4]",
    "hint": "Which probability or statistical model matches the information given? Which parameters or conditions must be identified before calculating?",
    "answer": "\\(\\frac{{{Σ}^{16}}_{i=1}{x}_{i}}{16}=14.5\\) (M1) Note: Award M1 for use of \\(x=\\frac{{{Σ}^{n}}_{i=1}{x}_{i}}{n}\\). \\(\\Rightarrow {{Σ}^{16}}_{i=1}{x}_{i}=232\\) (A1) new \\(x=\\frac{232-9}{15}\\) (A1) \\(=14.9 (=14.86,=\\frac{223}{15})\\) A1 Note: Do not accept 15. [4 marks]",
    "whereToLearn": "Mathematics: Analysis and Approaches Standard Level Course Companion · First edition, 2019\n\nWhole question §6.3 Measures of central tendency · p. 287",
    "teacherNote": ""
